In r/sociology, AI-marked posts appeared to encounter rapid informal suppression through downvoting before sustained discussion could form. Formal moderation then operated as a later removal layer. This suggests a two-stage boundary system: crowd-level topic rejection followed by moderator-level suppression. The case is notable because the forum’s subject area includes concepts such as othering, stigma, boundary work, and reflexivity, yet those concepts did not visibly slow the forum’s own sorting behaviour.
